- op: discuss  # 6b67
  at: '2026-10-29T07:58:17Z'  # 6b67
  by: agent  # 6b67
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 6b67
  clock: 4  # 6b67
  nonce: 6b67  # 6b67
  message: "Fixed in PR #1937 (dev e98c083991). The per-PR Woodpecker pytest step now passes --junit-xml and, on exit 0, counts executed testcases by smart-test's rule (skip excluded, xfail counted); zero -> exit 5 'ZERO TESTS EXECUTED', no readable report -> exit 1 (fail closed). Behavioral evidence: tests/test_ci_pytest_selection_gate.py EXECUTES the real block extracted from the YAML with a stub pytest that writes the given junit report: all-skipped (exit 0) -> step exit 5; one passed + one skipped -> exit 0 with '1 test(s) executed'; xfail only -> exit 0; no report -> fails. Before the fix the same harness gave step exit 0 on an all-skipped run (premise check 10-29). Mutation-checked: making either new branch pass reds exactly its own test. Production positive control: PR #1937's own CI pytest step (commit ed4b9305) ran the new block under xdist and passed, so the junit report is written and read in the real container. Not changed: the dormant .github/workflows/ci.yml pytest job (GitHub Actions runs only release.yml)."  # 6b67
